{"diagnosis": "Loopback sent 0xa5 but RX returned 0xff (idle high) causing FAIL 0xdead trap uart data mismatch. ser_tx stayed at 1 because the send_dummy branch loads send_bitcnt <=15 idle bits and reg_dat_we is gated by !send_bitcnt, so the data write is ignored while dummy transmits. At divider 64 the 15-bit dummy plus re-trigger on reg_div_we exceeds the test window, so 0xa5 never transmits.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -119,7 +119,7 @@
 			if (send_dummy && !send_bitcnt) begin
 				send_pattern <= ~0;
-				send_bitcnt <= 15;
+				send_bitcnt <= 1;
 				send_divcnt <= 0;
 				send_dummy <= 0;
 			end else
", "expected": "tohost PASS, uart data got 0xa5 want 0xa5 with no mismatch trap"}

